# Linux Filesystem Space Issues Impacting Monthly Patching

We are currently having filesystem space issues across several of our Linux servers. This is causing our Ansible patching jobs to fail, thus not completing our monthly patching activities.
1-	Filesystem Space Issues
The primary issues are with the /usr, /boot and /var filesystems.
1.1-	 /usr  (Linux Firmware Installation)
The package installation/upgrade fails because of insufficient disk space in the /usr filesystem. This is particularly the case with the linux-firmware package, which is a very large package.

