2. Connectivity Issues – Ansible Hosts Unreachable
Network connectivity and authentication issues are another major cause of Ansible patching failures. These occur when the Ansible controller cannot establish an SSH connection to the target Linux servers.
Potential causes include:
•	Incorrect firewall group or zone: Servers assigned to the wrong firewall security group, zone, or policy may block SSH connections from the Ansible controller.
•	Missing network routing: Missing or incorrect routes between the Ansible controller and target hosts can result in errors such as No route to host or Network is unreachable.
•	Firewall rules blocking SSH: Network firewalls, host-based firewalld, or iptables/nftables rules may prevent inbound SSH traffic on port 22.
•	SSH service issues: The sshd service may be stopped, failing, or listening on an unexpected port.
•	Incorrect IP address or DNS resolution: Outdated inventory records, incorrect IP addresses, or DNS resolution failures can cause Ansible to connect to the wrong destination or fail to locate the host.
•	Ansible account authentication issues: Incorrect SSH keys, expired or locked accounts, missing authorized keys, or AD/LDAP authentication problems may prevent the Ansible service account from logging in.
•	SSH access restrictions: Configuration settings such as AllowUsers, AllowGroups, or PAM access controls may deny access to the Ansible account.
•	Host unavailable: Servers that are powered off, undergoing maintenance, experiencing network interface issues, or otherwise unreachable will cause Ansible connection failures.
•	Incorrect Ansible inventory configuration: Invalid hostnames, incorrect ansible_host values, wrong SSH ports, or incorrect connection variables can prevent successful connections.
Common Ansible error messages:
UNREACHABLE! => Failed to connect to the host via ssh

ssh: connect to host x.x.x.x port 22: No route to host

ssh: connect to host x.x.x.x port 22: Connection timed out

ssh: connect to host x.x.x.x port 22: Connection refused

Permission denied (publickey,password)
